Test-only OpenCascade verification
---------------------------------
The application and default tests use SMLib. The separate
spice-cad-verification test package uses opencascade-rs 0.3.0 under
LGPL-2.1 and Open CASCADE Technology 7.8.1 under LGPL-2.1 with its exception.
This verification software makes use of facilities provided by Open CASCADE Technology.
https://github.com/bschwind/opencascade-rs
https://github.com/Open-Cascade-SAS/OCCT/tree/V7_8_1
See licenses/upstream/opencascade.txt, licenses/upstream/opencascade-sys.txt,
licenses/OCCT-LGPL-2.1.txt, and licenses/OCCT-LGPL-EXCEPTION.txt.
The complete application source and pinned rebuild inputs are provided by
this repository, Cargo.lock, and flake.lock; see docs/development.md for replacing
and rebuilding the reference libraries.

Test-only game import verification
---------------------------------
The standalone tools/game-import verifier vendors gltf-json 1.4.1 under
MIT OR Apache-2.0, with a scoped required-specular validator correction.
Its source record and both licenses are retained in
tools/game-import/vendor/gltf-json/. This dependency is not linked into Spice CAD.

Packaging
---------
Experimental AppImages use nix-appimage's AppRun and AppImage's type2 runtime
under MIT; see licenses/packaging/. The exact sources and build recipes are
pinned by the nix-appimage input in flake.lock. The AppImage additionally
bundles runtime/system libraries with their respective licenses.

Nix installs this notice, LICENSE, ASSETS.md, brand terms, and licenses/ under
share/doc/spice-cad. Keep them with redistributed builds. System libraries
provided by the Nix closure or operating system retain their own licenses;
redistributors of those libraries must preserve their accompanying notices
and comply with their source-distribution obligations.
